<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria BNP-Dresdner bank net profit 1.16 bln lvs.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria BNP-Dresdner bank net profit 1.16 bln lvs.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>BNP-Dresdner bank (Bulgaria) posted a 1.158 billion lev net profit for 1996 after setting aside provisions of 3.308 billion levs, the bank's profit-and-loss account published in the State Gazette showed.</p>
<p>BNP-Dresdner bank (Bulgaria) is the Bulgarian subsidiary of Banque Nationale de Paris, Dresdner bank and the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development.</p>
<p>Comparative figures for 1995 were not available.</p>
<p>Figures from the bank's annual profit and loss account and balance sheet follow in million levs unless stated otherwise:</p>
<p>							   1996</p>
<p> Total revenue				     5,530.277</p>
<p> Net income on financial oparations	  5,229.404</p>
<p> Business and administration costs	     479.194</p>
<p> Provisions					  3,307.653</p>
<p> Taxes						   285.103</p>
<p> Profit						1.157.750</p>
<p> Total assets				     15,207.158</p>
<p>Financial assets, including</p>
<p>extended interbank deposits and</p>
<p> lending to non-financial clients	   15,048.675</p>
<p> Non-financial assets				102.244</p>
<p>Attracted funds, including deposits from</p>
<p> financial and non-financial clients	 9,620.118</p>
<p>Capital, including shareholders equity</p>
<p> provisions and reserves			 5,251.827</p>
<p> Items not included in the balance *	 1,681.738</p>
<p>* Under local accountancy standards items not included in the balance comprise bank guarantees and other commitments issued by the bank. -- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 911 88</p>
</text>
